        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Look back at your predictions. What would you keep and what would you change?' Give WAIT TIME of 10-15 seconds. Ask: 'S and P differ in size and the distorted photo differs in size too. So what makes S and P similar but not the distorted photo?' Cold-call 3 learners, then ask 2 others to add on or disagree using 'I agree because...' or 'I disagree because...'. Point to the matatu: 'A real matatu is 700 cm and the model is 28 cm. Is the model similar? What stays the same?' Write the agreed class rule on chart paper: 'Similar objects have the same shape; only the size can be different.' Do NOT teach angle or ratio tests, but say: 'In Lesson 3 we will check this rule with numbers.' Also introduce 'congruent' (same shape and same size) briefly and contrast it with 'similar'.",
