        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Ms Wanjiru's board is our record of thinking. Write one thing we now know and one thing we still wonder. One idea per note.' Give 3 minutes. Invite 4 learners to post and read their notes. Ask: 'Which of our earlier questions has this lesson helped us answer?' WAIT TIME 10-15 seconds. Circle the area and cost questions and say: 'We now know lengths follow LSF. Next lesson we will test what happens to area and cost.' Do not answer the area question yet.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Driving Question Board as a public record: linking new questions to previous ones shows learners how today's evidence answers some questions and creates others, keeping the phenomenon in view.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Observe whether notes are linked to evidence (the 9 m tree, the 9 x 12 photo) and whether at least some learners raise the area/cost question without prompting. Count how many questions go beyond length (area, cost, volume)."
