        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Open your model from Lesson 4. Add what today's evidence lets you predict. Include one diagram and one rule.' Circulate and ask: 'If Mr Otieno gave you only the width of P, how would you find its height?' (k = 6/3 = 2, height 4 x 2 = 8 cm). WAIT TIME 10-15 seconds. Cold-call 3 learners to read their rule aloud. Close by asking: 'Lengths doubled from S to P. Does the cost, KES 30 to KES 120, just double? What do we need to find out?' Leave the question open for Lesson 6.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Cumulative model revision: adding to the same model each lesson shows learners how the evidence accumulates, and the 'Still to explain' box highlights the gap that Lesson 6 will address.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Check the model for: the correct rule (image = object x k; object = image / k), both worked examples with correct values (9 x 12 cm; 9 m tree), and a clear note that area and cost are not yet explained. Learners who can find the height of P from its width only demonstrate the transfer needed."
