    "overview": "Ms Wanjiru recalls Achieng's two prints in Kisumu. Mr Otieno made print P from print S and nobody told us where he scaled from or by how much. Learners first predict how we could find out when we only have the object and the image. They then gather evidence on coordinate grids: they plot triangle ABC with A(2,1), B(4,1), C(3,3) and its image A'(3,2), B'(7,2), C'(5,6), draw lines AA', BB' and CC', and see that all three lines meet at one point (1,0). They measure AB = 2 and A'B' = 4 and calculate k = 2. In the Explain phase they justify why the lines must meet at the centre, check with the distances from the centre, and apply the method to the photo case, where print P is the image of print S with k = 2. The DQB is updated with new questions and answers, and the class adds a third section to the enlargement model: how to recover the centre and the scale factor from an object and its image.",
