        "teacherMoves": "Say: 'Mr Otieno gave Achieng print P, but he forgot where he enlarged from and by how much. We only have the object and the image. What can we do?' Remind learners: 'In Lesson 8 and 9 we drew rays from the centre through each point. What if we draw those lines backwards?' Give 2 minutes of silent individual thinking, then pairs share. WAIT TIME: after asking 'Where might the centre be?' wait 10-15 seconds before taking answers. Cold-call 4 pairs and record all predictions on the board without judging. Ask: 'What would you need to measure to find the scale factor?' Wait 10 seconds and cold-call 2 learners.",
        "sensemakingStrategy": "Prediction with confidence rating (Predict-Observe-Explain). Writing a prediction and a confidence score makes learners' initial ideas visible, creates a reason to test them, and lets them see later whether their thinking has changed. Reasoning backwards from the finished image activates the Lesson 8-9 ray model.",
        "formativeAssessment": "Look for: learners who suggest joining corresponding points; learners who propose comparing lengths of corresponding sides; learners who suggest guessing a point 'in the middle' (misconception). Tally how many of the 4 pairs mention lines through corresponding points. Collect 5 prediction slips and record common ideas and misconceptions to revisit in the Explain phase."
